(intellectual eye. This expedition has been the favourite dream of my early years. I have) Tj
T*
(read with ardour the accounts of the various voyages which have been made in the prospect) Tj
T*
(of arriving at the North Pacific Ocean through the seas which surround the pole. You may) Tj
T*
(remember that a history of all the voyages made for purposes of discovery composed the) Tj
T*
(whole of our good Uncle Thomas' library. My education was neglected, yet I was) Tj
T*
(passionately fond of reading. These volumes were my study day and night, and my) Tj
T*
(familiarity with them increased that regret which I had felt, as a child, on learning) Tj
T*
(that my father's dying injunction had forbidden my uncle to allow me to embark in a) Tj
T*
(seafaring life.) Tj
ET
BT
/F1 10.5 Tf
0.043 0.051 0.075 rg
1 0 0 1 64 638.39 Tm
15.500 TL
(These visions faded when I perused, for the first time, those poets whose effusions) Tj
T*
(entranced my soul and lifted it to heaven. I also became a poet and for one year lived in) Tj
T*
(a paradise of my own creation; I imagined that I also might obtain a niche in the temple) Tj
T*
(where the names of Homer and Shakespeare are consecrated. You are well acquainted with my) Tj
T*
(failure and how heavily I bore the disappointment. But just at that time I inherited the) Tj
T*
(fortune of my cousin, and my thoughts were turned into the channel of their earlier bent.) Tj
ET
BT
/F1 10.5 Tf
0.043 0.051 0.075 rg
1 0 0 1 64 545.39 Tm
15.500 TL
(Six years have passed since I resolved on my present undertaking. I can, even now,) Tj
T*
(remember the hour from which I dedicated myself to this great enterprise. I commenced by) Tj
T*
(inuring my body to hardship. I accompanied the whale-fishers on several expeditions to) Tj
T*
(the North Sea; I voluntarily endured cold, famine, thirst, and want of sleep; I often) Tj
T*
(worked harder than the common sailors during the day and devoted my nights to the study) Tj
T*
(of mathematics, the theory of medicine, and those branches of physical science from which) Tj
T*
(a naval adventurer might derive the greatest practical advantage. Twice I actually hired) Tj
T*
(myself as an under-mate in a Greenland whaler, and acquitted myself to admiration. I must) Tj
T*
(own I felt a little proud when my captain offered me the second dignity in the vessel and) Tj
T*
(entreated me to remain with the greatest earnestness, so valuable did he consider my) Tj
T*
(services.) Tj
ET
BT
/F1 10.5 Tf
0.043 0.051 0.075 rg
1 0 0 1 64 374.89 Tm
15.500 TL
(And now, dear Margaret, do I not deserve to accomplish some great purpose? My life might) Tj
T*
(have been passed in ease and luxury, but I preferred glory to every enticement that) Tj
T*
(wealth placed in my path. Oh, that some encouraging voice would answer in the) Tj
T*
(affirmative! My courage and my resolution is firm; but my hopes fluctuate, and my spirits) Tj
T*
(are often depressed. I am about to proceed on a long and difficult voyage, the) Tj
T*
(emergencies of which will demand all my fortitude: I am required not only to raise the) Tj
T*
(spirits of others, but sometimes to sustain my own, when theirs are failing.) Tj
ET
BT
/F1 10.5 Tf
0.043 0.051 0.075 rg
1 0 0 1 64 266.39 Tm
15.500 TL
(This is the most favourable period for travelling in Russia. They fly quickly over the) Tj
T*
(snow in their sledges; the motion is pleasant, and, in my opinion, far more agreeable) Tj
T*
(than that of an English stagecoach. The cold is not excessive, if you are wrapped in) Tj
T*
(furs--a dress which I have already adopted, for there is a great difference between) Tj
T*
(walking the deck and remaining seated motionless for hours, when no exercise prevents the) Tj
T*
(blood from actually freezing in your veins. I have no ambition to lose my life on the) Tj
T*
(post-road between St. Petersburgh and Archangel.) Tj
ET
BT
/F1 10.5 Tf
0.043 0.051 0.075 rg
1 0 0 1 64 157.89 Tm
15.500 TL
(I shall depart for the latter town in a fortnight or three weeks; and my intention is to) Tj
T*
(hire a ship there, which can easily be done by paying the insurance for the owner, and to) Tj
T*
(engage as many sailors as I think necessary among those who are accustomed to the) Tj
T*
(whale-fishing. I do not intend to sail until the month of June; and when shall I return?) Tj
T*
(Ah, dear sister, how can I answer this question? If I succeed, many, many months, perhaps) Tj
