(How slowly the time passes here, encompassed as I am by frost and snow! Yet a second step) Tj
T*
(is taken towards my enterprise. I have hired a vessel and am occupied in collecting my) Tj
T*
(sailors; those whom I have already engaged appear to be men on whom I can depend and are) Tj
T*
(certainly possessed of dauntless courage.) Tj
ET
BT
/F1 10.5 Tf
0.043 0.051 0.075 rg
1 0 0 1 64 569.89 Tm
15.500 TL
(But I have one want which I have never yet been able to satisfy, and the absence of the) Tj
T*
(object of which I now feel as a most severe evil, I have no friend, Margaret: when I am) Tj
T*
(glowing with the enthusiasm of success, there will be none to participate my joy; if I am) Tj
T*
(assailed by disappointment, no one will endeavour to sustain me in dejection. I shall) Tj
T*
(commit my thoughts to paper, it is true; but that is a poor medium for the communication) Tj
T*
(of feeling. I desire the company of a man who could sympathise with me, whose eyes would) Tj
T*
(reply to mine. You may deem me romantic, my dear sister, but I bitterly feel the want of) Tj
T*
(a friend. I have no one near me, gentle yet courageous, possessed of a cultivated as well) Tj
T*
(as of a capacious mind, whose tastes are like my own, to approve or amend my plans. How) Tj
T*
(would such a friend repair the faults of your poor brother! I am too ardent in execution) Tj
T*
(and too impatient of difficulties. But it is a still greater evil to me that I am) Tj
T*
(self-educated: for the first fourteen years of my life I ran wild on a common and read) Tj
T*
(nothing but our Uncle Thomas' books of voyages. At that age I became acquainted with the) Tj
T*
(celebrated poets of our own country; but it was only when it had ceased to be in my power) Tj
T*
(to derive its most important benefits from such a conviction that I perceived the) Tj
T*
(necessity of becoming acquainted with more languages than that of my native country. Now) Tj
T*
(I am twenty-eight and am in reality more illiterate than many schoolboys of fifteen. It) Tj
T*
(is true that I have thought more and that my daydreams are more extended and magnificent,) Tj
T*
(but they want \(as the painters call it\) _keeping;_ and I greatly need a friend who would) Tj
T*
(have sense enough not to despise me as romantic, and affection enough for me to endeavour) Tj
T*
(to regulate my mind.) Tj
