(gentleness and the mildness of his discipline. This circumstance, added to his well-known) Tj
T*
(integrity and dauntless courage, made me very desirous to engage him. A youth passed in) Tj
T*
(solitude, my best years spent under your gentle and feminine fosterage, has so refined) Tj
T*
(the groundwork of my character that I cannot overcome an intense distaste to the usual) Tj
T*
(brutality exercised on board ship: I have never believed it to be necessary, and when I) Tj
T*
(heard of a mariner equally noted for his kindliness of heart and the respect and) Tj
T*
(obedience paid to him by his crew, I felt myself peculiarly fortunate in being able to) Tj
T*
(secure his services. I heard of him first in rather a romantic manner, from a lady who) Tj
T*
(owes to him the happiness of her life. This, briefly, is his story. Some years ago he) Tj
T*
(loved a young Russian lady of moderate fortune, and having amassed a considerable sum in) Tj
T*
(prize-money, the father of the girl consented to the match. He saw his mistress once) Tj
T*
(before the destined ceremony; but she was bathed in tears, and throwing herself at his) Tj
T*
(feet, entreated him to spare her, confessing at the same time that she loved another, but) Tj
T*
(that he was poor, and that her father would never consent to the union. My generous) Tj
T*
(friend reassured the suppliant, and on being informed of the name of her lover, instantly) Tj
T*
(abandoned his pursuit. He had already bought a farm with his money, on which he had) Tj
T*
(designed to pass the remainder of his life; but he bestowed the whole on his rival,) Tj
T*
(together with the remains of his prize-money to purchase stock, and then himself) Tj
T*
(solicited the young woman's father to consent to her marriage with her lover. But the old) Tj
T*
(man decidedly refused, thinking himself bound in honour to my friend, who, when he found) Tj
T*
(the father inexorable, quitted his country, nor returned until he heard that his former) Tj
T*
(mistress was married according to her inclinations. "What a noble fellow!" you will) Tj
T*
