(Yet do not suppose, because I complain a little or because I can conceive a consolation) Tj
T*
(for my toils which I may never know, that I am wavering in my resolutions. Those are as) Tj
T*
(fixed as fate, and my voyage is only now delayed until the weather shall permit my) Tj
T*
(embarkation. The winter has been dreadfully severe, but the spring promises well, and it) Tj
T*
