(paramount to that. My duties towards the beings of my own species had greater claims to) Tj
T*
(my attention because they included a greater proportion of happiness or misery. Urged by) Tj
T*
(this view, I refused, and I did right in refusing, to create a companion for the first) Tj
T*
(creature. He showed unparalleled malignity and selfishness in evil; he destroyed my) Tj
T*
(friends; he devoted to destruction beings who possessed exquisite sensations, happiness,) Tj
T*
(and wisdom; nor do I know where this thirst for vengeance may end. Miserable himself that) Tj
T*
(he may render no other wretched, he ought to die. The task of his destruction was mine,) Tj
T*
(but I have failed. When actuated by selfish and vicious motives, I asked you to undertake) Tj
T*
(my unfinished work, and I renew this request now, when I am only induced by reason and) Tj
T*
(virtue.) Tj
